<description>&lt;p&gt;Violent clashes continue between Viv Ansanm gangs and Haitian security forces, now reinforced by a Kenya-led multinational mission patrolling Port-au-Prince and Kenscoff. The Dominican army has supplied large ammunition stocks to the 400 Mawozo gang, boosting its firepower against security forces. Erik Prince is operating a private mercenary effort against the gangs, adding a new security dimension. The United Nations has allocated an additional US$75 million for life-saving aid to 507,000 people and renewed sanctions on Haiti for another year. The conflict has caused 193 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/10/1168598&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE1PSDNZYklwbFlURFR4ZWw5TXBzM2kxUUV5SEZfZHFESFdkUVU2Q2tKUHZJSzBNeFNGZmlfTUQtb0pzaFJZNllRRjNMajF1RkJBdkNkcGF4aHVabFF4TzNteUhEQWVsazkxMnhJeFdSZVZfekluWW8xZjJSX2VYQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Trinidad Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxQcWZDYXZPN0JidjVVNEZHQzdvY1FlSWhUX2hxdVJXZXFBQTBLUkpYSFFoVTNDT1ZZYmNWSEg3Ul9sUi01Q2hlckp1U0I0Q05vNFV4Vm1fNHVMZkM3UjNsVlJsUFgtcDlqeWZIdzdBRmQ1WDBGTkZpQ2thRjJmM3JBRjB2ZGFBS0M1OXBXQ1d6T2pRY2lXUjlYSHYycw?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxOblAzYVVTSXpuLUg3YUd2cGxYRTM0Rzd6MEh5aWNPSzN5OFgwT01wa2VXUjh4RHJPVkkyVE9JMjVLak9EVHpuZ0NRTFlsZXp4ZzYtQ05tYW1UNkNjMVdIWExiX3VGNHpLMWJPZ0ROQ3Q1ZExvVXJkVzRFbGtVSm5BQmQ3ekdhOGVNd01KTTZYOFViY2xSZFJobw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Eastern Herald&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizgFBVV95cUxPc2psaHhCWlBMMkRtY2FWaUd1MWMxYnFNVURFdzl5M1ZiOEw1U0plSFk0dXU0aE5DZE1TUUQwazRtb2VhU0ZsQnQwdW1UYU84aXFTXzVkanRTMG5HMkI1V2NWNUFkR2dfNmNaQ0pjbGlnd0NwbjU0bi1xW